# Stage 10 calibration comparison — run record

## Scope and safeguards

- Planned fixed base models: TabPFN 3.5 for `DEATH_BINARY` and `ZSN`, and
  preliminary Random Forest for `FIBR_PREDS`, per the Stage 10 direction.
- The script reads only explicit Stage 1 development artifacts, saved Stage 9
  OOF raw probabilities, and the Stage 3 source needed to reconstruct the
  preliminary Random Forest pipeline. It does not reference held-out paths.
- New outputs are isolated in `stage10_calibration_comparison_outputs/`; the
  script refuses to run if that directory already exists. No Stage 9 or prior
  outputs are modified. No dependency install, model-weight download, or
  external access is planned.
- Stage 9 raw outer OOF predictions and target-level seed-42 five-fold outer
  assignments are reused unchanged. For each target/outer fold, four inner
  fold-local model fits regenerate training-side scores for Platt, isotonic,
  constrained Beta, and temperature calibrators. Outer validation rows do not
  fit the calibrators.
- The provisional decision screen operationalizes “meaningful and stable” as
  at least 1% pooled improvement in both Brier and Log Loss and wins in at
  least four of five folds on both. Raw is recommended only when it has lower
  pooled Brier and Log Loss and wins at least four of five folds on both.
  Otherwise Platt is the default if alternatives are mixed or similar. This is
  descriptive, not a significance test.
- Beta calibration uses `scipy.optimize` with nonnegative coefficients on
  `log(p)` and `-log(1-p)`, enforcing a monotone mapping without an extra
  package. Temperature scaling uses a positive scalar on `logit(p)` with no
  intercept. All methods use the same outer raw probabilities.
- Full-development model/calibrator bundles will be prepared using the
  selected fixed base models and development OOF scores only. These artifacts
  do not authorize test access or constitute a one-time held-out evaluation.

## Preflight and helper tests

- `.venv/bin/python -m py_compile mi_stage10_calibration_comparison.py` —
  passed.
- `env SKB_DATA_DIRECTORY=/private/tmp/mi-stage10-skrub
  MPLCONFIGDIR=/private/tmp/mi-stage10-mplconfig .venv/bin/python -m unittest
  discover -s tests -p 'test_stage10_calibration.py' -v` — 8 tests passed.
- A no-fit preflight validated 9 checks: Stage 9 selected candidate OOF ID
  alignment, exact outer fold membership, and JSON-safe estimator parameter
  extraction for all three targets. It confirmed the Stage 10 output
  directory did not exist. No model fitting occurred in preflight.
- Initial checks captured package metadata already installed in `.venv`:
  scikit-learn 1.9.1, SciPy 1.18.1, TabPFN 9.2.0, and CatBoost 1.2.10.
  `betacal` is not installed and is not needed.

